From 9ac71404f47951ed5bc65582f03db6c087672fb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adit <adit@example.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:34:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hero): pop-up paper automaton theatre, run by a pull-tab

Replaces the sunrise with a multi-plane paper stage in a preserve-3d stack:
backdrop, paper gears, an arched frame, a blue ring, floor, clouds, the two
halves of an orange curtain and layered wings, with the sun demoted to a prop on
a string. The headline is two cardboard signs held with brass brads. Dragging
the PULSE. CAD frame (or pressing its PULL tab, which also works from the
keyboard) drives one 0-1 value: curtains and wings slide apart, gears turn, the
sun swings, and the INTERFACES letters fold forward on alternating creases. It
snaps open or shut on a spring.

Keeps the four data-hero-sticker stickers the gravity pit peels into About.
Pointer tilt, scroll lift and idle-pause move into the new hook. Removes the old
sunrise scene and its now-dead rules from the shared stylesheet. Rounds computed
SVG coordinates (hero and diorama gears) to fix a server/client hydration
mismatch from float formatting.
